%% programs/tests/neg_guard_boot/agent_boot.glp
%%
%% Negative fixture: an invalid guard in the agents' program of a
%% multi-isolate boot, the program directory agent/ beside this file ---
%% REPL :boot, IsolateManager with programDir.  Until 2026-11-10 the program
%% followed the boot clause in this file, which the loader now refuses.
%% GLP-Spec glp.tex, Definition "Guarded Clause": "G is a conjunction of guard
%% predicates"; true is no guard predicate of the catalogue (GLP-Spec
%% appendix-guards.tex) and no unit clause defines it, so the agent's load is
%% refused and the boot fails.  agent.glp beside it is the same agent program
%% as a module file, the one program an AgentRuntime runs.
%
%% The agents' program is the program directory agent/ beside this file,
%% which the agents load, this file carrying its boot clause and the persons
%% it names and nothing else (TGLP 6ce148a, modules.tex, "Entry and the
%% absence of a boot module"; IGLP, Implementation Notes, "Boot").

procedure boot.
boot :-
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice,
    say(alice, ch(_?, _))@alice.

%% The person at each agent: it tells the agent its name, and reads nothing.
exported procedure say(Constant?, Channel(Stream(Constant), Stream(Constant))?).
say(P, ch(_, [P?])).
